Question 1 — Mixed Concepts

Using the employees and departments tables:

Find the department name and the average salary of that department, 
but return only those departments whose average salary is greater than ₹70,000. 
Sort the result from highest average salary to lowest.

SELECT d.DepartmentName AS DepartmentName,
ROUND(AVG(e.Salary),2) AS AverageSalary
FROM departments d
JOIN employees e
ON e.DepartmentID = d.DepartmentID
GROUP BY d.DepartmentID
HAVING AVG(e.Salary) > 70000
ORDER BY AVG(e.Salary) DESC;
